            <div xml:id="d770">

                <pb facs="0826" n="722" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg722"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Manchuria/149: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Acting Secretary
                            of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-04-25T11:00:00+08:00">April 25, 1932—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 25—3 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>464. The following from American Consul General at Harbin: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“April 23, noon.</p>
                        <list>
                            <label>1.</label>
                            <item>Vice Consul Takigawa stated
                                that yesterday Japanese troops after one hour’s fighting with old
                                Kirin troops near Imienpo caused them to retreat and that early this
                                morning 3,000 brigands attacked <pb facs="0827" n="723"
                                    xml:id="pg723"/> the town and occupied the Chinese Eastern
                                Railway station at Sanchaho, 102 kilometers south of Harbin, thus
                                holding up traffic for a few hours.</item>
                            <label>2.</label>
                            <item>Traffic on eastern line still suspended. Soviet management has
                                promised to furnish necessary rolling stock for transportation of
                                Japanese troops.”</item>
                        </list></quote></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
